abstract: >-
  HDBLAST is a speculative, testable research hypothesis asking whether a gravitational event in
  a fifth dimension could have transferred energy into our four-dimensional universe and started
  the hot Big Bang. The program registers a five-dimensional Einstein–scalar shell model and
  publishes exact and numerical results, scoped error bounds, negative results and corrections.
  September 2026 checkpoints correct the static late-time branch and propose a matter extension.
  October research adds conditional source/operator bounds, finite-band error identities and
  enclosures for a prescribed continuum Bunch–Davies prehistory target at nine fixed momenta,
  followed by certified comparisons at all 49,152 original stored capsule-node occurrences.
  Exact continuous-time incoming-error transport is conditional on fixed finite weights and
  identical subsequent forcing and complete contacts. Independent implementations and portable
  replays preserve these results. Later numerical trajectories and the full twelve-case
  continuous pressure/contact/time/momentum/ultraviolet certificate remain unresolved. Metric
  calibration remains failed. No hot Big Bang cause or observational signal is established;
  external novelty is not assessed.
